WEBVTT

00:11:59.652 --> 00:12:01.196
that are not really fair, right?

00:12:01.220 --> 00:12:04.624
Because you don't really
get what their situation is

00:12:04.648 --> 00:12:06.042
in the same way as you would

00:12:06.066 --> 00:12:07.987
if you were working face-to-face.

00:12:08.011 --> 00:12:10.056
AG: Think about your virtual team.

00:12:10.080 --> 00:12:11.985
Shared identity and shared understanding

00:12:12.009 --> 00:12:13.746
are pivotal for trust.

00:12:13.770 --> 00:12:17.616
How do you make that happen when
you're not in the same physical space?

00:12:17.640 --> 00:12:19.378
You might strengthen shared identity

00:12:19.402 --> 00:12:21.255
by circulating feedback from customers

00:12:21.279 --> 00:12:24.073
on why your team's work is
more important than ever.

00:12:24.581 --> 00:12:26.775
And you could get to
some shared understanding

00:12:26.799 --> 00:12:29.596
by talking about your favorite
video conference bloopers.

00:12:29.620 --> 00:12:32.571
Some of you have been experimenting
with other strategies.